# Siblings the CI gate checks out (at origin/master) next to this repo so the
# wallet's cross-repo tests resolve them deterministically.
#
# xchain-sdk: the wallet composes every action through it.
#
# xchain-documentation: test/unit/ActionManifestConformance.test.js compares the
# vendored test/fixtures/action-manifest.json against the canonical
# ../xchain-documentation/protocol/action-manifest.json. That test SKIPS when the
# sibling is absent, so an undeclared dependency does not fail loudly - it fails
# only when some OTHER repo's gate run happens to have left a checkout at the
# venue's work/xchain-documentation, and then the byte-identity guard silently
# compares against that leftover revision instead of canonical. Observed exactly
# that way: a wallet push failed on a CI runner against a docs sibling one
# commit stale, while the same suite was green locally and had passed on another runner.
# Declaring it makes the harness ship the canonical origin/master copy and rm -rf
# any leftover, so the guard runs against the single source of truth.
xchain-sdk
xchain-documentation
